vine 1.2.0
prefix: mem
title: bounded large-origin embedding and allocation evidence
---
[root] Bound large-origin embedding memory (complete)
Issue #3 reports multi-gigabyte native memory while one large origin is embedded.
Run the issue sequence in evidence order and give the Grimoire benchmark a
shape-aware allocation view that can show how an inference microbatch change
moves logical memory without pretending to predict an OS allocator.
The plan has three separate evidence layers: deterministic Grimoire-derived
memory projections, exact scry-owned logical byte observations, and diagnostic
native process-memory observations. They must not collapse into one score.
The production fix remains one-origin atomic: all final embeddings for an
origin are prepared before that origin becomes visible, and cross-origin
batching is not introduced by this plan.
Files: memory.vine is the plan; performance.md is the root evidence log for
this investigation; the child tasks own implementation and evidence files.
Do: execute the graph in dependency order; keep the existing v1 artifact and
set-upsert semantics intact unless a task records an explicit reviewed change.
Accept: the large-origin path has a measured baseline, a tested bounded
microbatch implementation or a visible blocker, a Grimoire memory artifact
whose units and assumptions are auditable, and a final disposition for ORT
allocator and staging alternatives.
-> checkpoint
-> checkpoint-followup
@guidance text/markdown docs/benchmarks.md
@guidance text/markdown performance.md
@guidance text/markdown docs/product-planning/architecture.md
@guidance text/markdown agent-proposed-specs/set-upsert.md
@guidance text/plain benchmarks.vine
