[microbatch] Bound raw inference output by microbatch (complete)
Change the scry embedding path so fastembed does not retain raw ONNX outputs for
all spans in one origin before pooling them.
Serves: large single-origin add can process bounded inference batches while
retaining only the final vectors needed for one atomic record.
Absent: a smaller batch argument passed to one fastembed call still leaves
`EmbeddingOutput` holding every internal `SingleBatchOutput` until the call
finishes.
Known by: a validated microbatch size, one fastembed invocation per submitted
microbatch, immediate conversion to final embeddings, exact final vector count,
and unchanged add failure and visibility behavior.
Files: crates/scry/src/embed.rs, crates/scry/src/benchmark.rs,
crates/scry/src/add.rs, and focused tests beside those owners.
Do: keep `SlicedText` as the source of bounded passages. Split only the spans
belonging to the current origin, call fastembed separately for each configured
microbatch, pool and convert each result before the next call, and accumulate
final embeddings without writing the origin early. Start the comparison at a
validated default of 32 and retain 64 and 16 as measured alternatives; do not
batch passages from different origins. Define the private diagnostic meaning
of embedding invocation and microbatch counters without silently giving an old
field two meanings. Preserve the one-origin record and transaction boundary,
refusal continuation, failure halting, and bounded source policy.
Accept: small, multi-span, and scale cases produce exactly one final embedding
per span; a failed microbatch leaves the current origin uncommitted and applies
the existing later-member halt rule; search, provenance, refusal, and handle
behavior remain valid; focused tests prove the configured value is positive and
that a single fastembed call is never given the whole large-origin passage
list; add-only exact fingerprints and logical outcomes remain explainable.
-> contract
-> grimoire-memory
-> scale
> Store::add now processes SlicedText in validated 32-span calls, converting each result to final embeddings before the next fastembed call; all final vectors remain in memory until one atomic per-origin record commit.
> Benchmark-only --microbatch-size selects 64, 32, or 16 for separate scale runs. The identical 747-span fixture produced 1,228,500,992/1,432,776,704 bytes at 64, 713,588,736/808,693,760 at 32, and 457,883,648/495,513,600 at 16 for working set/private memory.
> Focused library tests (139), benchmark tests (8), add-only fingerprints/logical counts, memory-v1 exact check, v1 baseline check, and normal no-feature scry check pass; no cross-origin batching or partial visibility was introduced.
