[bounded-size] Enforce the safe microbatch range (complete)
Make the benchmark-selected passage microbatch obey fastembed's internal batch boundary.
Serves: the memory reduction cannot be bypassed by selecting a Scry microbatch larger than the retained internal batch.
Absent: `--microbatch-size 1000` silently recreates multi-batch raw-output retention inside one Scry call.
Known by: one validated range, one error path, the production default, and CLI behavior for zero and over-limit values.
Files: crates/scry/src/embed.rs, crates/scry/src/lib.rs, crates/scry-benchmarks/src/main.rs, focused tests beside those owners.
Do: enforce a positive size no greater than the pinned fastembed batch size of 256 before model work begins; expose only the benchmark-feature boundary needed by the CLI; reject invalid values visibly and keep the normal product API/default unchanged.
Accept: 1 and 256 are accepted, 0 and 257 are rejected, the scale CLI reports the selected value, and the bound has one owner rather than duplicated parser folklore.
-> microbatch
> The scale runner now requires observed embedding_calls and embedding_batches to equal ceil(span_count / configured_microbatch_size), so altered option wiring or default behavior fails visibly rather than passing on nonzero counts.
